@prompt
Hazel is a live functional environment. Every edit is a valid program, and it evaluates *around* holes (the hexagons), so you always see a result.

A plant drinks 250 ml a day. A week is `250 * 7`, plus a 50 ml top-up on the new moon. Fill the hole so the week comes to **1800**.

@hint
A week is 7 days.

@reference
### Holes
Hexagons are holes. Hazel evaluates around them. Fill one by typing a value.

### Integer operations
`(+ - * /)`

@hints
Fill the hole with `7`.

@code
250 * ¿ + 50

@test
test answer == 1800 end
